                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "varimotion":</h3><p>AKG&#8217;s <b>Laminate Varimotion</b> is a type of dynamic microphone membrane characterized by the lamination of two layers of plastic, one lightweight and the other dense, into a single-piece, variable-thickness piece. The thin outer edges allow for extended low-frequency response, while the thicker center of the membrane allows for high SPL handling. </p><p>The manufacturing process is patented in the US; see additional notes on the D7 page.</p><p>Read more about Laminate Varimotion on AKG&#8217;s <a href="http://www.akg.com/fbid/">Feedback is Dead</a> site.</p>
